{#
    Bottom-of-screen offer to turn on browser notifications.

    Rendered into every layout but shipped `hidden`: whether it applies is a
    client-side question (push supported? permission already answered? a
    dismissal from last week? a page that already has a push button?) and only
    the browser can answer it. `push-prompt.js` decides and removes `hidden`.

    The dismissal is a button rather than a link so it cannot become a
    dismissible-hijack target — the same reasoning as `app-install.twig`.

    Two fixed bars would overlap, so the two banners are mutually exclusive:
    when this one is visible the app-install bar is hidden by CSS. Dismissing
    this one hands the bottom of the screen back.
#}
<div id="push-prompt" class="push-prompt" data-push-prompt hidden>
    <button type="button" class="push-prompt-close" data-push-prompt-close aria-label="বন্ধ করুন">
        {{ icon('x', 'w-4 h-4') }}
    </button>

    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-neutral-900">নোটিফিকেশন চালু করুন</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500">অর্ডার ও রিচার্জের আপডেট ব্রাউজারেই পেতে অনুমতি দিন।</p>
            <p class="push-prompt-hint text-xs text-danger-600" data-push-prompt-hint hidden></p>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm shrink-0" data-push-prompt-allow>অনুমতি দিন</button>
    </div>
</div>